# This machine's own settings. Copy to `.env` and fill in what applies; git
# ignores `.env`. A variable set in the shell wins over this file.
#
# Where it goes depends on what reads it:
#   - The server in Docker: beside docker-compose.yml, which hands it to the
#     container (docs/INSTALL.md, "With Docker").
#   - The server run from a checkout, and the desktop build: the main
#     checkout. A worktree branched from it reads the main checkout's `.env`
#     when it has none of its own (apps/server/src/dotenv.ts,
#     scripts/dotenv.mjs).

# --- Desktop build (apps/desktop) -------------------------------------------
# The Apple Development certificate in your keychain, so a build on this Mac
# is the same app to the keychain every time (docs/INSTALL.md, "The desktop
# app"). Without it the build is ad-hoc and asks for the keychain password on
# every install. Find the name with: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
#CSC_NAME="Apple Development: you@example.com (TEAMID)"

# A release build instead: a Developer ID certificate as a file, and its
# password. Notarised as well when the three APPLE_ variables are set.
#CSC_LINK=
#CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=
#APPLE_API_KEY=
#APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
#APPLE_API_ISSUER=

# --- Server (apps/server) ----------------------------------------------------
# The time zone for the log and for the days the server counts by. Read by
# docker-compose.yml; outside Docker the computer's own zone applies.
#TZ=America/Toronto
# Where the music inbox and the database live. Docker sets both itself
# (/app/library, /app/data); the defaults elsewhere are in
# apps/server/src/config.ts.
#SELFMP3_LIBRARY_DIR=
#SELFMP3_DATA_DIR=
#SELFMP3_PORT=4600
# The HTTPS address in front of this server, which it cannot work out for
# itself: a Tailscale Funnel or a Cloudflare tunnel. The addresses it finds on
# this computer are all local and all `http://`, which is no use to a device
# somewhere else and is refused outright by the published app; setting this
# also lets the published app's origin call the server (docs/INSTALL.md). No
# trailing slash.
#SELFMP3_PUBLIC_URL=https://music.example.com
# Where you publish the app, if not the project's own Pages site: the server's
# page links there, and a public address lets that site call this server.
#SELFMP3_APP_URL=https://you.github.io/selfmp3
# The doorman this server checks sign-ins and reaches buckets through
# (docs/SYNC.md). Unset, the project's own; empty, none.
#SELFMP3_DOORMAN_URL=
# A token of your own for a server whose bucket is a folder
# (SELFMP3_CLOUD_DIR below), instead of the one it makes on first boot. A
# server working for Google accounts ignores it: each library there has its
# own token, kept in hub.json in the data folder
# (docs/features/shared-server.md).
#SELFMP3_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Smart features (docs/features/ai.md): any OpenAI-compatible endpoint that
# answers in a JSON schema. Unset, they are off and say so. cli-bridge
# (https://github.com/Xiao215/cli-bridge) serves one on the server itself, at
# 127.0.0.1:8787, through the Claude Code CLI signed in there. Leave the key
# empty unless you gave cli-bridge an API_KEY.
#SELFMP3_AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1
#SELFMP3_AI_API_KEY=
#SELFMP3_AI_MODEL_FAST=sonnet
#SELFMP3_AI_MODEL_SMART=sonnet

# A folder standing in for the bucket, for a server run without an account (the
# dev profile sets this; docs/SYNC.md). Relative to the data directory.
#SELFMP3_CLOUD_DIR=bucket

# The listening model (docs/features/audio-intelligence.md, "How songs sound").
# On by default; its files (about 750 MB) are downloaded the first time it is
# wanted, or read from a folder an export left them in (scripts/sound-models).
#SELFMP3_SOUND=false
#SELFMP3_SOUND_MODELS=/path/to/sound-models
#SELFMP3_SOUND_THREADS=2
